1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,100
Paying to file your taxes?

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:08,508
Lots of people pay for tax prep they could get free. Here are the free options, and the upsells to watch for.

3
00:00:08,928 --> 00:00:14,799
In our example, paid prep costs $150 a year. Over ten years, that's $1,500.

4
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:22,025
Here are three free routes. Rules and income limits change every year, so always check IRS.gov.

5
00:00:22,795 --> 00:00:24,691
Route one. IRS Free File.

6
00:00:25,111 --> 00:00:37,566
If your income is under the yearly limit, IRS Free File gives you guided tax software from partner companies at no cost. Start from IRS.gov so you land on the free version.

7
00:00:38,336 --> 00:00:40,705
Route two. Free File Fillable Forms.

8
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:50,139
There's no income limit. They're electronic versions of the paper forms. No hand-holding, so they suit simple returns and people comfortable with the forms.

9
00:00:50,909 --> 00:00:53,343
Route three. Free help from a real person.

10
00:00:53,763 --> 00:01:07,735
VITA sites offer free tax prep from IRS-certified volunteers, generally for people with low to moderate income, people with disabilities, and limited English speakers. TCE focuses on people sixty and older.

11
00:01:08,505 --> 00:01:09,548
Now, the upsells.

12
00:01:09,968 --> 00:01:20,813
Free versions of commercial software can switch to paid when you add a state return, certain forms, or a premium upgrade. And remember episode twenty: refund transfer fees.

13
00:01:21,233 --> 00:01:25,355
If a screen asks for money, stop, and check whether a free route covers you.

14
00:01:25,775 --> 00:01:26,638
So, this week.

15
00:01:26,798 --> 00:01:29,835
Gather your W-2s and 1099s.

16
00:01:29,995 --> 00:01:31,503
Check which free route fits you.

17
00:01:31,663 --> 00:01:33,511
E-file, with direct deposit.

18
00:01:33,671 --> 00:01:35,945
And give the refund a job before it lands.

19
00:01:36,715 --> 00:01:43,079
This is general education, not tax advice. The Paycheck Planner in the description helps you plan the refund.

20
00:01:43,499 --> 00:01:46,959
Subscribe. Next time: how much car you can really afford.
